## Star Wars:  where it all lives
// Two servers other people run, and what each holds.  What's drawn and done with them is in StarWars.spellml.
// `star wars` is what this wrote, from looking at the server:
//   spell place ingest https://swapi.py4e.com/api --into StarWarsApi.spell --name "star wars"
// `spell place ingest --update StarWarsApi.spell` looks again, and changes only this file.
//
// Star Wars and its pictures belong to Lucasfilm and Disney, the words to Wikipedia's writers.
// They're asked for as it runs, never kept here, and the page says where they come from.

star wars is a web server at "https://swapi.py4e.com/api":
	- its id is its "url"
	- its rows are its "results"
	- its next page is its "next"
	- check it every 86400 seconds
	- characters live at "/people"
	- planets live at "/planets"
	- films live at "/films"
	- species live at "/species"
	- vehicles live at "/vehicles"
	- starships live at "/starships"
	- a character's hair color is its "hair_color"
	- a character's skin color is its "skin_color"
	- a character's eye color is its "eye_color"
	- a character's birth year is its "birth_year"
	- a planet's rotation period is its "rotation_period"
	- a planet's orbital period is its "orbital_period"
	- a planet's surface water is its "surface_water"
	- a film's episode id is its "episode_id"
	- a film's opening crawl is its "opening_crawl"
	- a film's release date is its "release_date"
	- a species's average height is its "average_height"
	- a species's skin colors is its "skin_colors"
	- a species's hair colors is its "hair_colors"
	- a species's eye colors is its "eye_colors"
	- a species's average lifespan is its "average_lifespan"
	- a vehicle's "cost in credits" is its "cost_in_credits"
	- a vehicle's max atmosphering speed is its "max_atmosphering_speed"
	- a vehicle's cargo capacity is its "cargo_capacity"
	- a vehicle's vehicle class is its "vehicle_class"
	- a starship's "cost in credits" is its "cost_in_credits"
	- a starship's max atmosphering speed is its "max_atmosphering_speed"
	- a starship's cargo capacity is its "cargo_capacity"
	- a starship's hyperdrive rating is its "hyperdrive_rating"
	- a starship's mglt is its "MGLT"
	- a starship's starship class is its "starship_class"

a "character" is a thing:
	- it lives in star wars
	- its "name" is text
	- its "height" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "mass" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "hair color" is text
	- its "skin color" is text
	- its "eye color" is text
	- its "birth year" is text
	- its "gender" is text
	- its "homeworld" is a planet
	- its "films" is a list of films
	- its "species" is a list of species
	- its "vehicles" is a list of vehicles
	- its "starships" is a list of starships
	- its "created" is a date
	- its "edited" is a date

a "planet" is a thing:
	- it lives in star wars
	- its "name" is text
	- its "rotation period" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "orbital period" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "diameter" is a number  // written as text there
	- its "climate" is text
	- its "gravity" is text
	- its "terrain" is text
	- its "surface water" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "population" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "residents" is a list of characters
	- its "films" is a list of films
	- its "created" is a date
	- its "edited" is a date

a "film" is a thing:
	- it lives in star wars
	- its "title" is text
	- its "episode id" is a number
	- its "opening crawl" is text
	- its "director" is text
	- its "producer" is text
	- its "release date" is a date
	- its "characters" is a list of characters
	- its "planets" is a list of planets
	- its "starships" is a list of starships
	- its "vehicles" is a list of vehicles
	- its "species" is a list of species
	- its "created" is a date
	- its "edited" is a date

a "species" is a thing:
	- it lives in star wars
	- its "name" is text
	- its "classification" is text
	- its "designation" is text
	- its "average height" is a number  // written as text there;  "n/a", "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "skin colors" is text
	- its "hair colors" is text
	- its "eye colors" is text
	- its "average lifespan" is text
	- its "homeworld" is a planet
	- its "language" is text
	- its "people" is a list of characters
	- its "films" is a list of films
	- its "created" is a date
	- its "edited" is a date

a "vehicle" is a thing:
	- it lives in star wars
	- its "name" is text
	- its "model" is text
	- its "manufacturer" is text
	- its "cost in credits" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "length" is a number  // written as text there
	- its "max atmosphering speed" is a number  // written as text there
	- its "crew" is a number  // written as text there
	- its "passengers" is a number  // written as text there
	- its "cargo capacity" is a number  // written as text there;  "none", "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "consumables" is text
	- its "vehicle class" is text
	- its "pilots" is a list of characters
	- its "films" is a list of films
	- its "created" is a date
	- its "edited" is a date

a "starship" is a thing:
	- it lives in star wars
	- its "name" is text
	- its "model" is text
	- its "manufacturer" is text
	- its "cost in credits" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "length" is a number  // written as text there
	- its "max atmosphering speed" is text
	- its "crew" is text
	- its "passengers" is a number  // written as text there;  "n/a", "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "cargo capacity" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "consumables" is text
	- its "hyperdrive rating" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "mglt" is a number  // written as text there;  "unknown" reads as nothing
	- its "starship class" is text
	- its "pilots" is a list of characters
	- its "films" is a list of films
	- its "created" is a date
	- its "edited" is a date


## Wikipedia:  a page each, by its name.  Not every name has one
wikipedia is a web server at "https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1":
	- check it every 86400 seconds
	- wiki pages live at "/page/summary"
	- a wiki page's id is its "pageid"
	- a wiki page's about is its "description"
	- a wiki page's summary is its "extract"
	- a wiki page's "content urls" is its "content_urls"

a "wiki page" is a thing:
	- it lives in wikipedia
	- its "title" is text
	- its "about" is text
	- its "summary" is text
	- its "thumbnail" is a thumbnail
	- its "content urls" is a page address book

// What's inside a page's answer, read in words:  `the source of its thumbnail`
a "thumbnail" is a thing:
	- its "source" is text

a "page address book" is a thing:
	- its "desktop" is a page address

a "page address" is a thing:
	- its "page" is text
